  "description": "An all-time classic, the 27.5” Fuzz has been around for a while and has proven itself in the world of racing, pro freeriding and everyday use. It’s been flipped and whipped by world class athletes at Freeride events around the globe, while it’s also a favorite for rental stations! It's easier to throw around than the 29” version making it a better choice for riders who want a more agile bike. It's low and slack and has chainstays that are proportional in length to the frame size. The eccentric headset allows for 16mm of reach adjustment. The Horst Link suspension uses a floating shock design thanks to which it was possible to achieve a low centre of gravity. Significant rearward movement in the axle path smooths out square faced impacts.\nINTENDED USE CATEGORY 7: DOWNHILL, FREERIDE & ENDURO\nTough alloy frame with double pass welds\nRadical geo w/adjustable reach\n200mm travel front and rear\nRock Shox Boxxer select Rc fork\nSRAM GX 10spd derailleur\nPowerful SRAM Guide RE brakes\nOFFSET HEADSET CUPS ALLOW REACH TO BE ADJUSTED\nReach can be adjusted by +/- 8mm.\n4-BAR HORST LINK SUSPENSION\n4-BAR HORST LINK SUSPENSION with unique floating shock design\nMODERN GEOMETRY\nOne of the most progressive on the market",
